A||||2||WisconsinGT||Need some answers...
Z||000000||WisconsinGT||08-05-99||11:40 PM||||to the following questions.<p>1. How do you clean the odometer numbers? (Especially the white 10th of a mile part)<p>2. I am getting used exhaust mnafolds that have the reinforced welding. What type of paint do I use? Should I give them a coat of primer?<p>3. I have white smoke coming out of the exhaust upon starting. (After sitting for awhile) It lingers in the air for awhile. So I knoe it is not water vapor. I checked the radiator it is full and looks very clean. I know that a cracked head could be one of the problems. But what else could cause this?<p>4. Why do mechanics look the other way or have dollar signs in their eyes when they see a Fiero and their owner?<p>5. I have a mechanic that is going to work on my 88GT. I have three (That I know of) broken exhaust manafold bolts. We agreed on taking off the heads. for two reasons. The bolts and to check for cracks. He made it quite clear that he is also going to clean the throttle, fuel injectors, pocket port the heads,  and put on new spark plug wires and plugs. Do I need to have all of this done? At $39 an hour I fear a very high bill. Or is he a competent mechanic that does the job right? Thanks folks!
Z||000001||JetroGT||08-06-99||01:38 AM||||I know that I'm repeating my self. Oh well. <br>When I had the top half of my V6 done. I already had all of the parts ready for the mechanic to use. Revalved heads, 2 new factory manifolds $$$$!!!, complete felpro head gasket set, reworked/polished throttle w/painted cooling lines and thermostat housing. . blah blah blah. To make a long story short, they quoted me a total price of $650. for the labor and that it would take 1 week. I ended up paying $985. and it took them 1 1/2 weeks. While they were in there I had them replace the alternator too. Was it worth it? I thik it was. I now have zero smoke on startup and increased horse power. When I got the car back I fixed the minor things that they missed. I did it myself because of past experiences. They forgot to install the heat shield on the alternator, the speed sensor was not plugged in, they ran the spark plug wires in the wrong place, did not bolt down the heat shield on the Y pipe. <p>Oh and expect to replace your EGR Senolid and or valve. I don't know why but I have had this done twice on different fieros and I ended up replacing the same parts.
Z||000002||Dan||08-10-99||09:04 AM||||Exhaust smoke is considered in three colors.<br>White is vapor, blue lingers and is oil probably time to rebuild heads with smoke at startup.Consider porting and polishing heads.<br>Great performance gain for low bucks and can be easily done yourself. Third color is black<br>which indicates overrich fuel or ignition problems.
